# Keep secrets out of the image and the build context small. GitLab #39 Stage 1.
#
# DELIBERATELY MINIMAL. An over-eager exclude here fails at 04:00 in production, not at build
# time, and the first draft of this file proved it: excluding `docs/` would have broken every
# run, because `docs/competition_registry.yml` is read at runtime by `registry.py:56` and by
# both contract-check scripts the entrypoint calls. Nothing is excluded here unless it is a
# secret, a build artefact, or large AND provably unread by the nightly.

# SECRETS — the one that matters most. `.env` holds API_FOOTBALL_API_KEY. The container gets
# that value from Secret Manager at runtime; baking it into a layer would make it readable by
# anyone who can pull the image, and it would survive rotation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*-key.json
*credentials*.json

# GitLab #74: CI-generated GCP credentials, written by `.gitlab-ci.yml`'s `.gcp_auth` anchor to
# $CI_PROJECT_DIR at runtime — never committed, but `*credentials*.json` above only catches ONE
# of the two files it writes. `build:nightly-image` builds this image with kaniko from that same
# directory, so without this the live bearer token gets baked into the built image (readable by
# anyone who can pull it, and it survives rotation same as any other secret).
#
# THIS IS THE ONLY GUARD on the kaniko path, not one of two. Round-1 review of the kaniko
# redesign (cto-reviewer + platform-reviewer, opus) corrected an earlier version of this comment
# that credited `.gcloudignore` as a second layer here — kaniko reads `.dockerignore` for its
# build context and has no concept of `.gcloudignore` at all (that file matters only for the
# human-run `gcloud run jobs deploy --source .` fallback in deploy/nightly/README.md, a
# completely different upload path CI never uses). Do not "tidy away" either entry here as
# redundant with `.gcloudignore` — it would silently reopen this exact leak.
.gcp-oidc-token
.gcp-credentials.json

# The v2 site (1.4M + node_modules when present) and the frozen legacy site. Astro apps the
# nightly never touches. `deploy:export` / `deploy:site-v2` are separate GitLab jobs and are
# not part of this image.
site_v2
site

# Build artefacts and caches — regenerated in the container, and a stale host copy is worse
# than none. `dbt deps` runs in the entrypoint, so dbt_packages must NOT be shipped.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
venv
dbt_project/target
dbt_project/dbt_packages
dbt_project/logs

# Agent governance and VCS metadata. Not read by any runtime path.
.git
.claude
.cursor

# KEPT ON PURPOSE, because the nightly reads them:
#   docs/           — competition_registry.yml (registry.py:56, check_layer_contract.py,
#                     check_registry_var_sync.py)
#   scripts/        — both contract checks run in the entrypoint
#   dbt_project/    — the models, seeds and packages.yml the prod build needs
#   ingestion/      — the pipeline itself
#   requirements.txt — the same file CI installs
